Raised/recorded: 2026-10-06 (America/Los_Angeles). Parent: #1202; global umbrella #7. Source-only milestone 2 packet, maximum two focused PRs.

Investigate four exact gap candidates along the Norway–Sweden boundary as one coordinated source/contact family. This is a bounded batch selected from the complete worldwide inventory, not a claim that repairing this border completes the global campaign. The root's preliminary native/coarse assessment is documented in #1202 comment 6025743744; use the already merged complete geometry inventory under #1164 as the authoritative baseline for this packet.

Observed, not approved: root authenticated both complete consumed simplified source files at geoBoundaries commit `9469f09592ced973a3448cf66b6100b741b64c0d` against the immutable registry. Their recorded vintages are Norway 2013 and Sweden 2017. Exact Shapely comparison of all four contact subjects found their atlas geometries differ from the consumed source geometries. Each candidate has positive-area overlap with the union of those four original source subjects, but most of each candidate remains outside that union. These observations establish neither an execution cause nor genuine land/water or boundary authority; independently reproduce them.

The recorded preparation pipeline `scripts/prepare.mjs` uses mapshaper `-simplify 25% keep-shapes` and `precision=0.0001`, followed by later repair/topology and geographic preparation. Treat this as a reproduction hypothesis: the original full input closure, executed code/runtime and intervening steps have not been bound for these candidates. A four-feature or two-country experiment cannot silently stand in for the original whole-world preparation.

Existing broader regional source/semantic packets #336 and #337 remain separate and open. Their reviews do not automatically establish these gap causes. Preserve their scopes/claims, consume verified related findings, and create one coordinated engineering follow-up only when supported; never assign competing unilateral boundary fixes.

Acceptance:
- Authenticate every complete component and original fragment/contact/water-diagnostic row by exact immutable file and feature bindings. Keep all four contact subjects; preserve positive-length versus point-only contacts and every unknown.
- Capture and authenticate both actual simplified source products, distinguish them from advertised full products, and verify source role, dates, precision, licenses and lawful authoritative references. Record incomplete retrievals honestly.
- Reproduce actual source-versus-atlas geometry differences and every candidate's exact intersections/differences without snap, buffer, simplification, MakeValid, coordinate normalization, minimum-area exclusion, or nearest fill. Store complete result geometries and guards, not only bounds or booleans.
- Examine existing complete independent water diagnostics and appropriate authoritative water/boundary evidence. A geometric overlap alone is not a real-world water verdict or approved territory assignment.
- Classify every scoped candidate into supported source mismatch, supported processing loss, supported physical water, mixed evidence, or explicit unresolved evidence. Preserve unknown portions; do not present an all-unknown initial collection as a completed correction.
- If a defect is established, specify the complete coordinated source/neighbor closure and propose a bounded engineering repair with exact before/after geography, native-grid, release/crosswalk/content revalidation and independent review requirements. Do not change core geometry here.
- Independent exact-head substantive review and normal serialized integration are required. Preserve unique evidence/failed attempts and release the worker's exact managed checkout when finished.

Immutable geometry baseline: `79ffb2ed04702e16f009e4675a8d74ef9bd09d4f`. Original comparison vintage: `cea80a8aa1f8a55ccb448a8f2ff71e10c49a26f1`; preserve their distinction. The legacy canonical-grid pin below is context only, not a new native measurement. Location identity and geography history must remain intact.

